    "summary": "One of seven anthropomorphic figurines, these <em>minkisi</em> contained medicines in which an ancestral spirit was believed to reside. <em>Minkisi</em> were objects of communal use; if conflict arose between two citizens, the Nkisi figure, along with the <em>nganga</em> (ritual leader) helped resolve the dispute. This small figure belonged to “the sorcerer of Loango,” chief of all sorcerers of that region (a province and port in West Central Africa).",
